{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ca96fe3d-1f25-457b-83f2-7a9b761eb792","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause of the Issue\n\nWhen Vibe starts up, its headless startup routine checks for default credentials (such as `MISTRAL_API_KEY`). Because the environment passed into the sandbox by [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-fg4dyh/run-vibe.sh) is sanitized with `env -i` and only passes `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, Vibe falls back to querying the macOS Keychain for credentials using `/usr/bin/security`.\n\nHowever, the sandbox configuration in [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-fg4dyh/agent.sb) explicitly forbids executing `/usr/bin/security`:\n```scheme\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n```\n\nExecuting `/usr/bin/security` is therefore blocked by the macOS sandbox with `[Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`, terminating Vibe with exit code `2`.\n\n---\n\n### Fix Applied\n\nIn [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-fg4dyh/run-vibe.sh), we added `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` to the environment passed into `sandbox-exec`:\n\n```bash\n( cd \"$W\" \u0026\u0026 env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" TERM=\"${TERM:-dumb}\" LANG=\"${LANG:-en_US.UTF-8}\" HOME=\"$SH\" VIBE_HOME=\"$VH\" \\\n    OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1 \\\n    sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/agent.sb\" \\\n    \"$VIBE\" -p \"$PROMPT\" --model devstral --auto-approve --trust --output streaming --output-dir \"$VH/out\" \\\n...\n```\n\n`VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` instructs Vibe's credential management (in both the Rust binary and Python runtime) to skip attempting to query the macOS Keychain via `/usr/bin/security`, allowing Vibe to run cleanly with `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.\n\nThe detailed analysis and explanation have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-fg4dyh/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":404.172162,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":300318,"output_tokens":10105,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":3738725,"total_tokens":310423}}}
